Subject: [PATCH 109/162] hjviewer: review fixes, style2 lane (1.9)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

U50, U51 (tests): the new hjviewer_dialog_frame_test.dart, which needs the
generated bridge, checks the real themes: MyTheme.lightTheme and darkTheme
(hjvRestyle) give a desktop's Elevated, Outlined and Text buttons a height of
36 and 16 at the sides at the platform's compact density, so that a padding
or minimumSize in hjv_theme.dart's styleFrom calls can no longer beat
kHjvDesktopButton unseen; and msgboxIcon's 22 px icon sits in one row with
the title, the text below at the full width. For that, msgboxContent's frame
is hjv_style.dart's HjvAlertContent (the same layout; msgboxContent gives it
the translated words), which hjviewer_style_test.dart also tests without the
bridge. hjviewer_style_test.dart checks too that a stacked HjvCallout with an
Elevated and an Outlined action is as high under the compact theme as under
kHjvDesktopButton's.

U45 (nit): the core's error toast is read out after the word for an error
(translate('Error'), 오류), so that a screen reader does not hear it as a
notice: hjvShowToast's dangerWord.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
